        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 24 at 2:01PM AST until September 24 at 4:30PM AST by NWS San Juan PR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive
rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Aguadilla in Puerto Rico...
Camuy in Puerto Rico...
Isabela in Puerto Rico...
Moca in Puerto Rico...
Quebradillas in Puerto Rico...
San Sebastian in Puerto Rico...

* WHEN...Until 430 PM AST.

* IMPACTS...Rises in small streams and normally dry arroyos.
Dangerous flows over low-water crossings. Water over roadways.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 200 PM AST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. These thunderstorms are moving northwestward
towards Aguadilla. This will cause urban and small stream
flooding. Up to 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Please report observed flooding to local emergency services or law
enforcement and request they pass this information to the National
Weather Service when you can do so safely.</instruction>
